{
  "title": "Hemangioma of Soft Tissue",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8069/hemangioma-of-soft-tissue",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 5 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Hemangioma of Soft Tissue is a benign vascular neoplasm that may be located in a cutaneous, subcutaneous, or intramuscular location.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition is typically seen in patients < 30 years of age who present with a painful mass of variable size depending on activity level.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with MRI with contrast.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually a trial of observation, NSAIDs, vascular stockings, and activity modification. Embolization, sclerotherapy, or surgical resection are indicated for lesions associated with persistent symptoms not responsive to nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "males and females incidence is equal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**<1% of all benign vascular tumors**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in patients **<30 years of age**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "intramuscular is commonly found deep in the lower extremities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most commonly found as isolated lesions, except for **diffuse hemangioma,** a rare childhood form which extensively involves a single limb",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "common in the hand",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8069/images/clinical%20image%20of%20hand%20hemangioma.jpg",
                  "caption": "hand hemangioma on 30-year-old female since birth (cutaneous cavernous hemangioma of the hand)"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Types",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may be **cutaneous, subcutaneous, or intramuscular**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**capillary (superficial) or cavernous (deep)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "caused by an **error in the new formation of a segment of the vascular system**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hormones may play role in modulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "20% are associated with **trauma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**pain** of variable intensity depending on activity level",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "symptoms of vascular engorgement if hemangioma is large",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**aching**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**heaviness**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**swelling**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "examine patient in both supine and standing position",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lower extremity lesions will fill up after several minutes of standing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**mass** of variable size depending on activity level",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8069/images/clinical%20image%20of%20cavernous%20hemangioma.jpg",
                      "caption": "Clinical photograph of a leg with cavernous hemangiomas (grape-like)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiograph",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may show small **phleboliths** (calcifications) inside the lesion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8069/images/benign%20cavernous%20hemangioma%20x-ray.jpg",
                  "caption": "x-ray of forearm demonstrating phlebolith associated with benign cavernous hemangioma"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "erosion into adjacent bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI with gadolinium",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8069/images/hemangioma%20mri%20forearm.jpg",
              "caption": "sagittal T2 of forearm showing benign hemangioma treated by simple resection"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**differentiates these benign lesions from arteriovenous malformations and angiosarcomas**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**iso- to hyperintense to muscle of T1- weighted imaging, hyperintense to muscle on T2-weighted imaging**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "focal areas of low-signal are a sign of blood flow or calcifications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "heterogeneous lesion with numerous small blood vessels and fatty **infiltration** (**bag of worms**)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Histology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**gross**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8069/images/gross%20image%20of%20hemangioma.jpg",
                  "caption": "Gross image of hand hemangioma being removed from thenar eminence"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**varies depending on whether it is capillary type or cavernous type**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**color spectrum varies from red to tan to yellow**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**micro**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8069/images/low%20power%20histology%20of%20hemangioma.jpg",
                  "caption": "low-power microphotograph of benign hemangioma"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**no malignant cells** noted by cellular pleomorphism noted",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "many **vascular dilations with large nuclei filled with erythrocytes**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "vascular **lumens infiltrated with muscle** fibers (intramuscular type)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cavernous shows large vessels with lots of fatty tissue",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Other vascular malformations",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arteriovenous malformations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "cavernous hemangiomas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "angiomatosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "vascular ectasia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sarcoma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "important to distinguish from sarcoma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation, NSAIDS, vascular stockings, and activity modification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "childhood lesions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "sclerotherapy or embolization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "performed by interventional radiology (IR)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**large, painful lesions** that fail NSAID and vascular stockings therapy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "marginal excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**small lesions of the hand**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "wide surgical resection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "lesions resistant to nonoperative management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "high incidence of **local recurrence**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Kasabach-Merritt syndrome**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare complications caused by entrapped platelets leading to a possbly fatal coagulopathy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Infantile hemangiomas involute by age 7**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**No incidence of malignant transformation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
